re exactly the blocks that hold a copy of the input; every other block is blank.\n- Pair 3: input row 1 is all 4s, and output block-row 1 (rows 4–7) is four copies side by side. Row 0 is all 0, and block-row 0 is empty.\n- Pairs 4 and 5 follow the same pattern.\n\nThe fact sheet says the \"background\" of pairs 1, 4 and 5 is the coloured value, because it is the most common one. Despite that, 0 is always the empty colour, in both the inputs and the outputs. So the rule tests for \"non-zero\", not \"not the background\".\n\n**Rule**\nFor each input cell (i, j): if it is non-zero, copy the whole input into output block rows 4i…4i+3, columns 4j…4j+3. Otherwise leave that block as 0.\n\n**Applying it to the test input**\nThe test input is\n\nThe non-zero cells are (0,1), (0,3), (1,0), (1,1), (1,3), (2,0), (2,1) and (3,3). The output gets a copy of the input in each of those 8 blocks and zeros in the other 8.\n\n**Teaching stages**\n1. Allocate an empty 16×16 canvas of zeros.\n2. Fill the four block-rows one at a time, stamping the input into every block whose input cell is non-zero, and emit after each block-row.\n\nThe canvas after block-row 3 is the final answer.","code":"def transform(grid):\n    g = np.array(grid)\n    h, w = g.shape\n    out = np.zeros((h * h, w * w), dtype=int)\n    emit(out, \"Allocate an empty canvas h*h by w*w: one input-sized block per input cell.\")\n    for i in range(h):\n        for j in range(w):\n            if g[i, j] != 0:\n                out[i*h:(i+1)*h, j*w:(j+1)*w] = g\n        emit(out, f\"Block-row {i}: stamp a copy of the input into each block whose input cell in row {i} is non-zero.\")\n    return out\n","candidate_tactics":{"selection":[{"source":"final explanation","text":"The fact sheet says the \"background\" of pairs 1, 4 and 5 is the coloured value, because it is the most common one."}],"template":[{"source":"final explanation","text":"This is a self-similar \"fractal\" enlargement: the 4×4 input acts both as a stamp and as the map that says where to put it."},{"source":"final explanation","text":"Fill the four block-rows one at a time, stamping the input into every block whose input cell is non-zero, and emit after each block-row."},{"source":"verified program checkpoint","text":"Block-row 0: stamp a copy of the input into each block whose input cell in row 0 is non-zero."}],"crop":[{"source":"final explanation","text":"- Every output is exactly 4× the input, 16×16."},{"source":"final explanation","text":"Allocate an empty 16×16 canvas of zeros."},{"source":"verified program checkpoint","text":"Allocate an empty canvas h*h by w*w: one input-sized block per input cell."}]},"provenance":{"reference_assisted":false,"query_labels_used_for_rule_diagnosis":false},"artifact_sha256":"02ebe57ec541a71cb430ccc61346db5d42ed7c5aa18ba06aaf0228c40e29ded1","task_sha256":"eaf6dfa5230da8ab28e251d081cc2a7c912b9e97be3f16466c1d9333bd8e4b17","validation":"Frozen corpus recorded successful replay on teaching fixtures; synthetic generalization not established."}
